	SetTerm -- By Brian C. White			-- Copyright (c) 1991 by Dynamic Software SystemsSetTerm is a program to allow easy changing of the "TERM" environmentvariable.  It also copies the chosen termcap entry into the "TERMCAP"environment variable so programs can access it much faster.  This issupported by the Microware "termlib" library, so all programs linkedwith that will make use of this feature.This archive contains:	copying			- Rules on copying (GNU General Public License)	readme			- this file	setterm			- 68000 executable code	setterm.c		- C source code for SetTerm	sys.setterm		- "/dd/sys/setterm" information file for setterm	termcap.extra	- Additional termcap entriesThis is version 1.21 of SetTerm.  Documentation is provided within the"setterm.c" and "sys.setterm" files.Please let me know if you have any comments, suggestions, gripes, etc.										Brian C. White------------------------------------------------------------------------------| OOOO   OOOO  OOOO |                Dynamic Software Systems                || O   O O     O     |--------------------------------------------------------|| O   O  OOO   OOO  | P.O.  Box 1565  | Delphi:    BRIANWHITE                || O   O     O     O | Esterhazy, Sask | CIS:       70313,3344                || OOOO  OOOO  OOOO  | S0A 0X0  Canada | Internet:  70313.3344@compuserve.com |------------------------------------------------------------------------------